<title>NETHERLANDS: P&amp;O Nedlloyd among top four container shippers.</title>
<headline>P&amp;O Nedlloyd among top four container shippers.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koninklijke Nedlloyd Groep NV and Peninsular and Oriental Steam Navigation Company Plc said their new container shipping joint venture P&amp;O Nedlloyd Container Line would rank among the world's top four.</p>
<p>It gave the following global rankings:</p>
<p>Standing container slots operated:</p>
<p>    P&amp;0 Nedlloyd					224,000</p>
<p>    Maersk						210,000</p>
<p>    Evergreen					   209,000</p>
<p>    Sea-Land					    198,000</p>
<p>Loaded twenty foot equivalent units (TEUs) per year:</p>
<p>    Maersk					     2,600,000</p>
<p>    Evergreen					  2,400,000</p>
<p>    P&amp;0 Nedlloyd				     2,300,000</p>
<p>    Sea-Land					   2,300,000</p>
<p>NOTES - Maersk Line is a unit of Dampskibsselskabet Svendborg A/S which in turn is a unit of privately owned Danish shipping and energy group A.P. Moeller.</p>
<p>Evergreen Marine Corp (Taiwan) Ltd is a Taiwanese based container shipping company.</p>
<p>Sea-Land Service Inc. is a unit of CSX Corp. of the United States.</p>
<p>Twenty foot equivalent units (TEUs) are the standard measure of volume in the container shipping industry.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
